# NEXUS AutoBuilder Pattern - System-Wide Rule

NEXUS must apply execution-builder patterns to **all systems**, not only PRISM.

## Applies To
- GPSS
- DDCSS
- PRISM
- ATLAS
- VERTEX
- COMPASS
- Future modules

## Required Pattern

For any request/workflow, enforce:
1. Prompt -> structured plan
2. Plan -> auto-generated artifacts
3. Artifacts -> executable tasks with owner/date
4. Execution -> health metrics + blocker tracking
5. Outcome -> learning updates for future cycles

## UX Rule

- No dead-end outputs.
- Always provide next best action.
- Prefer one command that generates all required operational artifacts.

## Control Rule

- Every module must include release gates before completion.
- Every module must report throughput, quality, cycle time, and financial impact.

## Integration Rule

Use shared object keys (`opportunity_id`, `client_id`, `contract_id`, `workflow_stage`, `owner`, `risk_score`, `margin_score`) across modules.
